<%# The O/H/L/C and volume of one bar (CKP-2), read as one inline line next to
    the range control — the shape every chart puts there.

    D93 pinned this to the latest bar and answered "what did the last session
    do". D112 adds the question it did not consider — "what did THAT day do" —
    so the strip follows the crosshair and falls back here when the pointer
    leaves. The server still paints the latest bar: it is what a reader sees
    before touching anything, and what they get back when they let go.

    D10: the card's heading already declares the currency, so the rows drop the
    prefix. Repeating `USD` four times is what that rule exists to stop.
    Locals: bar. %>
<dl class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1 font-mono">
  <% chart_stat_values(bar).each_with_index do |value, index| %>
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-1">
      <dt class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-fg-subtle">
        <%= t("market.precio.ohlc.#{MarketHelper::OHLC_KEYS.fetch(index)}") %>
      </dt>
      <dd class="text-xs font-semibold text-fg-default"
          data-chart-target="stat"><%= value %></dd>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</dl>
